I got stuck while parsing the `x` definition:

I just saw a type annotation indented 4 spaces, so I was expecting to see the
corresponding definition next with the exact same amount of indentation.

    greet : string -> string
    greet name =
        "Hello " ++ name

The top line is an optional type annotation. It works as compiler-verified
documentation and often improves error messages!
